21. Minimum data extract
Closed issues in the pilot domain across the full history: the fields in section 10, status and rating history, date history, scope references.
Issue-to-action cross-references, action tables with status history and cancellation reasons.
Incidents for the pilot domain’s in-scope processes across the full history (needed for P1 windows): the fields in section 11.
Process hierarchy and application inventory, for scope entity names and descendant matching.
Taxonomy dictionaries and the change log of field definitions and closure requirements, to define eras.
Owner identifiers in a restricted layer only (section 22).
For pilot selection: a one-week profile of three candidate domains against eligible case count, narrative quality, link coverage, impact, process and application references, SME availability, taxonomy quality and sponsor. Payments is one candidate and not assumed.

Controls on the extract: owner identifiers sit in a restricted source layer, excluded from embeddings, prompts and features, not shown in outputs except for authorised routing, with access logged and a written prohibition on use in ranking or comparison. Personal names in free text are scrubbed before any embedding or prompt.

